# The trust boundary: files that decide what the agents may do, what CI checks, what ships, what is spent, which
# identity the crew acts as, and what the security docs promise (docs/DELIVERY.md, sections 5 and 10).
# Everything else has no code owner, so the Foundry's approved work still merges by itself once green.
# This only takes effect when the ruleset on main turns on "require review from code owners"
# (.github/rulesets/main-own-identity.json), which waits until no agent acts as Nikita: the Claude Code sessions still
# open their pull requests as Nikita, and nobody can be asked to review their own work.
/.github/                     @nikitapage10
/.claude/                     @nikitapage10
/CLAUDE.md                    @nikitapage10
/vercel.json                  @nikitapage10
/package.json                 @nikitapage10
/package-lock.json            @nikitapage10
/api/_world/budget.ts         @nikitapage10
/api/_security/               @nikitapage10
/api/_github.ts               @nikitapage10
/scripts/foundry-watch.sh     @nikitapage10
/scripts/foundry-issue.sh     @nikitapage10
/docs/SECURITY.md             @nikitapage10
/docs/THREAT-MODEL.md         @nikitapage10
/docs/DELIVERY.md             @nikitapage10
